 "provenance": {
  "bays": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "THE MODULES MOUNT ON THE FRONT PLATE, NOT INSIDE IT. The front view punches four openings 3.54in [90] across and 1.42in [36] tall; a module's 108.97 plate covers its opening, its thumb-knobs landing in the pair of holes either side (3.91in, 99.4 apart on the panel drawings), and only the adapter block behind passes through. So each bay is the module plate's 108.97 x 35.05, centred on its opening, and `opening` is the hole an empty slot shows. Adjacent plates stand about 1.0 apart. every FHD cassette and adapter panel this library models is in every bay's `accepts`. FS states it on this datasheet's features list ('Compatible with all FHD cassettes and panels') and prints the same loading list with every one of them as fs/fhd-1ufce does; the module face is one 4.29 x 1.38in (108.97 x 35.05) envelope."
  },
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "spec table: 1.73 x 19.00 x 8.93in (44 x 482.6 x 227). The top view gives 17.64in [448] across the patch plate, 4.29in [107] in front of it to the D-rings and 4.64in [120] behind it to the lacer bar - 227 overall, the depth taken."
  },
  "cutouts": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "the fixed-plate family's four 90.0 x 36.0 openings on the 110.0 pitch (fs/fhd-1ufmt-s@1), less 17.3 into this 448 face; p3 prints 3.54in [90]."
  },
  "d-rings": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "the five D-rings and the lacer panel stand 107 in front of the plate; they are cable management, which the modelling guide does not draw. Noted, not placed."
  },
  "ears": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "drawn as common/rack-ear@1 outside the body under `ears`."
  },
  "envelope-faces": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "top, bottom, left and right are the envelope; the lacer bar and D-rings are not drawn."
  },
  "method": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "from fhd-1ube-fiber-enclosure-datasheet.pdf: p3 front view, p4 top view, p2 spec table. The patch plate is the fixed-plate family's stamping, as on the modular frame."
  },
  "model": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "FS's product page calls 72910 the FHD 1U rack mount blank enclosure; the datasheet title reads FHD-1UBE and its header FHD-FPP5DRL. `model` takes the title; the header is an alias."
  },
  "rear-opening": {
   "confidence": "drawing",
   "note": "THE BACK IS OPEN: the assembly illustration (p3) shows a patch plate, a front lacer panel and a rear lacer bar and no enclosure, so a module's back is seen from behind. One hole per front slot in the rear view, mirrored, running the 227 less a 1.0 plate, with the backs projected into them where each module's own body stands, as fs/fhd-1ufce's are; the real opening is the whole back."
